"""Saved-scene and web-app-state checks for Blender-family tasks.

A Blender desktop task ends with the scene saved to a ``.blend`` file.  This
module opens that file in a background Blender process and reads the resulting
scene document: render settings, object transforms, materials, modifiers, light
and camera data, viewport visibility, and the object-type census of the scene.

An OpenBlender web task ends with the app state stored in the browser Local
Storage document ``openblender.localState.v1``: the active project, its output
and render settings, its view layer, and every object with its transform,
material and modifiers.

The declared expectations are compared field by field: strings exactly, numbers
within the declared tolerance, and booleans exactly.  A missing or unreadable
``.blend`` file or app-state document is reported as a plain failure because the
scene the task asks for has not been produced.
"""

